WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.110
Speaker 1: in light of the anti vaccine problem
that we have in the United States, which may

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.950
well prevent us from really getting past this
pandemic, there are now more and more people

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:15.340
calling for mandatory that's government mandated
vaccination.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.820
Now, I want to be really clear.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:23.900
There is a huge difference between required
to do something and straight up compelled

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.220
vaccination.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.729
In other words, we've had for a long time
vaccines that are required.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:35.420
If you want to go to a certain college to
send your kid to a certain school, to work

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.329
in certain places, that wouldn't be new.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:44.920
What people are now actually talking about
more seriously, some people that's not predominant

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.789
is the idea of government actually mandating
that people must be vaccinated, period.

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:52.940
You have to just get the vaccine, a government
mandated vaccine.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.010
There's an op ed in The Washington Post by
Max Boot, who some people hate, called Stop

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.329
pleading with anti vaccines and start mandating
vaccinations.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:04.280
Now, there are really two parts here.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:10.000
First of all, is the question of would a mandatory
vaccine be legal now as a federal government

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.550
mandate?

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:16.120
There does not appear to be precedent for
that, that, you know, sometimes when we talk

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:21.720
about whether something would be legal, the
language should not be it doesn't seem like

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:27.220
it would be legal, but rather we're not able
to find precedent that that would be legal

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.460
at the state level.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:33.950
The answer appears to be that, yes, state
government in many states could mandate vaccination.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.480
You look at Jacobson v. Massachusetts from
nineteen five.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:45.470
That was a Supreme Court case in which the
court upheld the authority of states to enforce

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.360
compulsory vaccination laws.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:54.480
The court at the time articulated the view
that individual liberty is not absolute and

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.320
is subject to the police power of the state.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.660
Quote, Massachusetts was one of only 11 states
that had compulsory vaccination laws.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:06.060
Massachusetts law empowered the Board of Health
of individual cities and towns to enforce

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.690
mandatory free vaccinations for adults over
age 21.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:16.650
If the municipality determined it was necessary
for the public health or safety of the community.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.690
If you refused, you have to pay a five dollar
fine in nineteen two.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.890
Faced with the outbreak of smallpox, the Board
of Health of the City of Cambridge adopted

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:33.640
a regulation ordering the vaccination or vaccination
of inhabitants, basically pointing out that

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:40.030
this is part of preserving liberty when there
is a public health imperative.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:46.830
So legally, it's certainly conceivable that
states which wanted to make the covid vaccine

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.310
mandatory could do it.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.950
Then you would get into questions like does
it apply to people who are legally residents

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.090
of the state?

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.710
What if you're traveling through?

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.990
What if you're temporarily working in a particular
state?

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.610
There's a ton of complexity.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.810
That's not really the issue for me.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.860
I am not actively for mandatory vaccination.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:12.180
I'm for informing people and encouraging vaccination
in other ways.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.630
But it would be political suicide to try to
make the covid vaccine mandatory.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.420
Many of the people who don't want to get vaccinated
really don't want to get vaccinated.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:27.300
And I believe it would be unmitigated political
disaster for anyone who tries to push mandatory

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.300
vaccination.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:34.390
Now, one other thing in terms of the current
Supreme Court, my guess is that the current

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:41.230
court would only go with the precedent of
states being able to mandate vaccination.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:45.740
And if and when these vaccines are fully approved
by the FDA.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:50.360
My instinct is that if a state tried to do
this and there was a lawsuit and an appeal

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.970
and an appeal, and it eventually got to the
Supreme Court that the Supreme Court is not

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:59.140
going to uphold the precedent when it comes
to an emergency use authorization.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:06.209
I just don't imagine that one idea I had which
I tweeted about was this is now other ways

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:07.770
to get people vaccinated.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:15.080
I tweeted, If a rumor started that liberals
want to keep the vaccine away from conservatives

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:20.169
so that they die, would it make them get vaccinated
to own the Libs?

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:26.849
This is really childish reverse psychology,
but at the same time, it's this type of thing

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:33.289
that seems far more plausible and maybe even
more effective than a government mandated

00:04:33.289 --> 00:04:34.289
vaccination.

00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:36.229
I would be curious to hear from you.

00:04:36.229 --> 00:04:42.610
We've been talking about this week what if
the vaccines were marketed as the Trump vaccine,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:47.979
as Trump juice, as a freedom vaccine or whatever
the case may be?

00:04:47.979 --> 00:04:52.229
Would that maybe get some of these people
to go out and get vaccinated when it comes

00:04:52.229 --> 00:04:56.970
to mandatory vaccinations, even if you can
find legal precedent for it?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:02.659
I don't think it's the way to go in particular
because the backlash and people who figure

00:05:02.659 --> 00:05:09.590
out a way to avoid it anyway and the potential
politically suicidal aspect of it, it doesn't

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.830
seem like the way to go.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.530
I want to hear from you, though.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.009
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman
and let me know your thoughts.

